package wk:place;

/// The place itself, as a node. (`world` is a WIT keyword, so the interface
/// calls it a place; on the canvas the node is `world`.) It reads a glTF/GLB
/// out of its own vfs —
/// whatever you wire into it: a bind mount, a volume, another node's wk:fs —
/// and publishes it through `wk:scene` as scenery: geometry you walk through
/// rather than click. Re-reads the file as it changes, so editing the world
/// swaps it under your feet without a restart.
///
/// wk has no built-in world. A workspace surrounded by a plaza is a workspace
/// with one of these wired up.
world place {
    import wk:scene/scene;

    export run: func();
}
